;IN THIS FLUORESCENT PROTEIN THE CHROMOPHORE MOIETY FORMED FROM RESIDUES LEU66-TYR67-GLY68, (0YG66), UNDERGOES HYDROLYTIC DEGRADATION THAT RESULT IN PEPTIDE BOND CLEAVAGE OF THE PROTEIN BETWEEN RESIDUES 66 AND 67 AND ALSO DECARBOXYLATION OF LEU66.HERE, LEU66 IS CLEAVED OUT FROM THE CHROMOPHORE, DECARBOXYLATED BUT REMAINS ATTACHED TO PHE65. DEGRADED CHROMOPHORE MOIETY IS COMPOSED OF RESIDUES TYR67-GLY68 ONLY
;
